# tests/bash-tool, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. Five dispatches and their values — nothing a client is needed
# for. `bash-tool` resolves to the built worker by being named; `ws` is the
# workspace it operates on, checked in with its modes (run.sh is 100755, which
# is what the exec-bit assertion is about).
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --tool:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash-tool --ws:@=ws
